# Chakra Sentinel configuration. Installed to /etc/chakra/sentinel.conf.
#
# Sentinel works fully offline out of the box: a deterministic
# pattern-matching Intent Engine routes your question to one of the
# Chakra system API tools (chakra-health, chakra-processlens, etc.),
# runs it, and shows you the result. No setup, no internet, no API key.
#
# The EXPLAIN LAYER is OPTIONAL and OFF by default. If you set an API key
# below, Sentinel additionally sends the ALREADY-COLLECTED tool output to
# a hosted LLM and asks it to explain the result in plainer language. The
# LLM never decides which tool runs or gets raw system access -- it only
# ever sees data the deterministic, Risk-0-only dispatcher already
# fetched. This matches the master manual's own AI safety principle:
# AI -> Structured Intent -> Policy Validator -> Approved Chakra API,
# never AI -> raw shell.
#
# Queries you send to a hosted LLM leave this machine. If that's not
# acceptable, leave every key blank -- Sentinel stays fully functional.
# No key is ever shipped in the Chakra image; bring your own.
#
# The provider is auto-picked: Gemini if GEMINI_API_KEY is set, else NIM
# if NIM_API_KEY is set, else offline. Pin one with SENTINEL_LLM below
# (gemini | nim | none).

SENTINEL_LLM=

# --- Google Gemini --------------------------------------------------
# Free API key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey  (Google account).
# Any current model works; gemini-2.0-flash is fast and free-tier friendly.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash
GEMINI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta

# --- NVIDIA NIM ---------------------------------------------------------
# Free API key: https://build.nvidia.com  (NVIDIA account).
NIM_API_KEY=
NIM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct
NIM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
